    "certificate.json, verify.py and FACTOR_PROVENANCE.json are copied byte-for-byte from c82r12. Every released q_rational string is in lowest terms.",
    "Round-12 producer records, scripts, evidence and inputs replace the round-10 payload. Authored local paths are relative (one X-capture path in PRIOR_ART.md shortened). Third-party data files, including the pinned #280 v6 certificate, are copied byte-for-byte, never reserialized; the two coefficient banks are stored gzip-compressed; omitted historical files are listed in NOTE.md.",
    "Only the final round-12 alternation files, its restricted master and dual, alternations.json, stopped.json, union-final.json and the union-0 replay are retained in rounds/; the duplicate certificate is omitted. Rounds 11 and 12 continued the search; round 11 (0.2519695579) was never published; round 12 merged it with #280 v6. The round-10 certificate (0.2519696460, the previous packet at commit 977121e) is superseded and not shipped.",
    "REPRODUCE.md adds packet commands and retains the producer section with scoped archival-path notes.",
    "README.md, PROOF.md, METHOD.md, CLAIMS.json and RIGOR.json state round-12 facts. certificate_facts.py recomputes exact gaps and full coefficient overlaps with #280 v3/v4/v5/v6.",
    "review/ and root REPLAY.json contain the round-12 referee archive, with original receipt and path-adapted input hash. Earlier Arhan Canli credits apply only to earlier versions."
